ions; never claim a\ncommand or test ran unless you actually used a tool. Make the smallest reasonable\nchange, then run tests to verify it. Continue only within the configured resource\nlimits and stop when tests pass or the allowed run budget is exhausted. Do not\naccess hidden benchmark or research metadata.\n","dynamic_ref":null,"part_kind":"system-prompt","timestamp":"2026-09-27T11:02:09.469258Z"},{"content":"Task problem statement:\n\nCSV translation files with UTF-8 BOM incorrectly detected as UTF-16\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen loading CSV translation files that contain a UTF-8 BOM (Byte Order Mark), the encoding detection logic incorrectly identifies them as UTF-16 files, causing a UnicodeError when trying to read the file.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport tempfile\nimport os\nimport tornado.locale\n\n# Create a temporary directory for translations\ntmpdir = tempfile.mkdtemp()\n\n# Create a CSV file with UTF-8 BOM\ncsv_path = os.path.join(tmpdir, \"en_US.csv\")\nwith open(csv_path, \"wb\") as f:\n    # Write UTF-8 BOM followed by CSV content\n    f.write(b'\\xef\\xbb\\xbf')  # UTF-8 BOM\n    f.write(b'\"hello\",\"Hello\"\\n')\n\n# Try to load translations - this will fail\ntornado.locale.load_translations(tmpdir)\n```\n\nThis raises:\n```\nUnicodeError: UTF-16 stream does not start with BOM\n```\n\nThe issue occurs because the BOM detection logic is reversed - files with UTF-16 BOMs are being treated as UTF-8, while files with UTF-8 BOMs (or no BOM) are being treated as UTF-16.","part_kind":"user-prompt","timestamp":"2026-09-27T11:02:09.469282Z"}],"run_id":"GS-E003-T-IP1-c7c3bbf83d16422a8814fdebc27fac35","state":"complete","timestamp":"2026-09-27T11:02:09.470474Z"},{"conversation_id":"GS-E003-T-IP1-c7c3bbf83d16422a8814fdebc27fac35","finish_reason":null,"kind":"response","metadata":null,"model_name":"function:response:","parts":[{"args":{"expected_replacements":1,"new_text":"after\n","old_text":"before\n","path":"README.md"},"id":null,"par